Fix soundness issue in the Boogie type encoding that Dafny uses, whose reverse casts said that every value is an int (a bool, ...) and so had no model (boogie-org/boogie#1168): Dafny now builds against Boogie 3.5.5 with a fix, which emits no reverse casts and keeps the proofs that relied on them by passing a value of a built-in type to the solver as a cast; a proof may need a different amount of work, so a few proofs near a resource limit may now finish within it, and a few others may not
